Z||000000||MooCow||04-12-2001||05:11 PM||||Well Ed thinks that it is my ignition modual gone bad cause I dont have a spark on the coil.  The thing is that I have replaced it twice and it still does nothing.  So could it be the brand I am buying??  Ed told me to buy an A/C delco one.  So I will try that out tomorrow and see what happens.  Or could it be the wires that lead from the igniton modual to the coil itslef gone bad??  How do I test that?<P>                                  Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||04-12-2001||05:16 PM||||Take the modual to AutoZone and have them test.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||04-12-2001||05:51 PM||||The guy at AutoZone told me they could test it but only in the car.  I am not towing the car all the way donw there for them to test it.  Maybe the guy was just dumb  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>                             Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-12-2001||06:09 PM||||He must be dumb. Every AutoZone I've been to has the proper equipment to test ignition moduals out of the car, for free even.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||04-12-2001||10:54 PM||||MC - I had a similar problem.  The root cause was the short wire harness between the dist and the coil. It had a short in it but would sometimes connect sometimes short.  It drove me crazy for a couple of days.  A new part from the 'local' chevy dealer was $34. Ouch.  Anyway, you may want to check it out. Also, unplug you tack filter to see if that is bleeding.||||reg||3
Z||000005||tgowens||04-13-2001||12:32 AM||||Ken, you have changed the ignition module but have you changed the pick-up coil? (located under the dist. cap - green and white wires) - they can cause an ignition module to go bad - if the pick-up coil is bad and you don't change it you will continue to have the same problem no matter how many ignition modules you replace.......hope this helps....<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">         </A><P>87 GT - Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||04-13-2001||09:51 AM||||Yep I changed the pick up coil as well as the plugs and wires and distributor cap and rotor.  I will bring down the old igntion today to see if it is shot or not.  Where is the tach filter located??<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000007||tgowens||04-13-2001||11:50 AM||||should be mounted to the block somewhere alongside the distributor - looks like a small silver cannister slightly larger than a AA flashlight battery........||||reg||1
